===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|US}} A piece of paper given to students who are late to class.
#: {{ux|en|The teacher gave her a '''tardy''' because she did not come into the classroom until after the bell.}}
# {{lb|en|US}} An instance of a student's being marked as tardy by a teacher on the teacher's attendance sheet.

====See also====
* {{l|en|tardy slip}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete|transitive}} To make tardy.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Winter's Tale|3|2|passage= the good mind of Camillo '''tardied''' <br>My swift command}}
# {{lb|en|rare|intransitive}} To [[dawdle]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Donna Morrissey|title=Kit's Law|page=86
|passage=Sitting there on the rock behind the school, I heard nothing but the occasional raised voice of some youngster '''tardying''' on his way home, and the joints in the schoolhouse squeaking from the frost.}}

